Description: Biometric wakeups leave the display off until a match
 A device can declare the kind of its wakeups in the udev property
 POWERDEVIL_WAKEUP_TYPE (timer, powermanagement, network, telephony or
 biometric). Such a device counts as wakeup source when its event count rose
 during the sleep cycle: the wakeup count only counts while user space uses
 /sys/power/wakeup_count, which systemd does not do, so the detection of the
 wakeup source never matched.
 .
 After a wakeup by a biometric sensor the display stays off and the device
 goes back to sleep after 5 s without user input; the screen locker asks for
 a full wakeup on a match. A full wakeup (org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement.wakeup)
 now ends the wait for user input after any wakeup that left the display off
 and starts the usual display idle time; before, the device went back to sleep
 after the idle time even though the consumer had turned the display on, and
 the display then stayed on without idle timeout.
Author: pocket-debs
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
